course: dictionary
lesson: 5599
title: In lieu of
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: «Lieu» is a rare word. In English you will mostly meet it in two phrases: «in lieu» and «in lieu of». Both mean instead of, so one thing takes the place of another.
explain: «She worked six extra hours, so she took a free afternoon in lieu.» The extra hours were not paid with money. They were replaced by time off. The clue is that the sentence talks about extra work and then about a free afternoon.
explain: «He was paid in lieu of notice when his job ended.» Notice is the warning time you work before you leave a job. Swap your meaning into the sentence: he was paid instead of notice. It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: «In lieu of» means instead of, as in «juice in lieu of milk» (juice instead of milk).
fact: In English, «lieu» is only used in the phrases «in lieu» and «in lieu of».
fact: «Time off in lieu» (TOIL) is time given back to a worker for extra hours they have worked.
fact: «Payment in lieu of notice» is money paid instead of working the notice period when someone leaves a job.
fact: In French, «lieu» means place, as in «un lieu», but that is a different use. Do not use it to mean place in English.
exercise: «The school sent a letter in lieu of a phone call.» What does in lieu of mean? | Before | *Instead of | Because of | As well as
exercise: «She took a free afternoon in lieu of the extra hours she worked.» Find the phrase that shows one thing replaces another. | free afternoon | she worked | *in lieu of | extra hours
exercise: Ruby's dad says, «I'll have tea in lieu of cake.» What does he mean? | *He will have tea instead of cake | He will have cake and tea together | He will have no tea at all | He will share his cake with a friend
test: «He was paid in lieu of notice when he left.» What does in lieu of notice mean? | Notice given before he was paid | Extra notice on top of his pay | Free lunch at work | *Money instead of working the notice time
test: Which phrase means instead of? | *in lieu of | in charge of | in spite of | in case of
exam: «Ella was given time off in lieu of the hours she worked on Sunday.» What does in lieu mean here? | Before | Because of | Without any pay | *Instead of
